\fs36 \cf4 1. Executive architecture decision\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs19 \cf3 The programme should be engineered as two independently releasable products sharing contracts, event semantics and performance-domain data, not as one tightly coupled application. Blackstar AI owns natural-language-to-safe-tone control; LyricPilot owns local sung-position tracking and display. The shared Performance Event Bus is an optional integration seam rather than a runtime dependency for either V1 product.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa480\partightenfactor0
\cf3 The core safety pattern is a two-stage authority model. Probabilistic components may interpret language, speech or acoustic evidence, but they never directly change DSP state or invent live lyric content. Blackstar commits changes only through the deterministic Tone Compiler, Validator and atomic DSP bridge. LyricPilot commits display movement only through constrained Song Map candidates, jump protection and a tracking state machine.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\slmult1\sa480\partightenfactor0

